# Crossroads go every 30 cells, so the streets make a grid of squares. The
# third street runs into the main street, where its plot is free, and closes
# a loop with a crossroads.
> new empty
> free on
> construction off
> expect cannot build crossroads at s0:40 every 30 cells
  ok: can't build intersection at s0:40: Crossroads go only every 30 cells
> build crossroads at s0:61
  #1 intersection at s0:61-63, done
> ride #last
  rider: s0:62 facing +
> turn up
  rider: s1:131 facing +
> expect cannot build crossroads at s1:151 every 30 cells
  ok: can't build intersection at s1:151: Crossroads go only every 30 cells
> ride +30
  rider: s1:161 facing +
> build crossroads here
  #61 intersection at s1:160-162, done
> ride #last
  rider: s1:161 facing +
> turn up
  rider: s2:131 facing +
> ride +30
  rider: s2:161 facing +
> build crossroads here
  #106 intersection at s2:160-162, done
> expect streets 4
  ok: 4 streets
# three built, one made where the third street met the main street
> expect count crossroads 4
  ok: 4 intersection
> streets
  s0  runs east (lots on its north side), cells 10..252
  s1  runs north (lots on its west side), cells 10..252, from crossroads #1
  s2  runs west (lots on its south side), cells 10..252, from crossroads #61
  s3  runs south (lots on its east side), cells 10..252, from crossroads #106
    crossroads #1: s0:62 = s1:131 (cell A62)
    crossroads #61: s1:161 = s2:131 (cell AE62)
    crossroads #106: s2:161 = s3:131 (cell AE32)
    crossroads #107: s0:32 = s3:161 (cell A32)
